# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Vendored assets are hash-pinned: never touch their bytes.
#
# `* text=auto` with core.autocrlf=true rewrites these to CRLF in a Windows
# working tree. That changes their bytes, which changes their SHA-384, which
# means the integrity="sha384-..." attributes stop matching and the browser
# REFUSES TO EXECUTE THEM. On 2026-07-31 that presented as Alpine, DOMPurify,
# Lucide and JointJS all failing to load on a Windows checkout - the whole front
# end inert, every icon blank - while Linux and production were unaffected,
# because there the checkout is LF and the hashes match.
#
# The trap is that the obvious fix is the wrong one. Rehashing the templates
# against the CRLF copies makes a Windows checkout work and breaks every Linux
# deploy, production included. The bytes must simply never be rewritten.
*.min.js   -text
*.min.css  -text
app/static/vendor/** -text
app/config/api_contract_subset.yaml -text
